---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout title="FAQ | UI Forge" description="Frequently asked questions about UI Forge.">
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6 py-16 sm:py-24">
    <div class="grid gap-12 lg:grid-cols-[0.8fr_1.2fr] lg:gap-20">
      <header class="max-w-md">
        <span class="inline-flex rounded-full border border-white/10 bg-white/[0.03] px-3 py-1.5 text-xs font-medium uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-zinc-500">
          Help center
        </span>
        <h1 class="mt-6 text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight text-white sm:text-6xl">
          Questions, answered.
        </h1>
        <p class="mt-6 text-lg leading-8 text-zinc-400">
          A quick guide to using, customizing, and sharing UI Forge components.
        </p>
        <div class="mt-10 border-l border-indigo-400/50 pl-4 text-sm leading-6 text-zinc-500">
          Can't find what you need? Check the component documentation for
          installation commands, examples, and props.
        </div>
        <a
          href="/docs"
          class="mt-7 inline-flex text-sm font-medium text-zinc-200 underline decoration-white/20 underline-offset-4 transition-colors hover:text-white hover:decoration-white/50"
        >
          Browse the documentation
        </a>
      </header>

      <div class="faq-list divide-y divide-white/10 rounded-2xl border border-white/10 bg-white/[0.02]">
        <details open class="faq-item group">
          <summary class="faq-summary">
            <span>What is UI Forge?</span>
            <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
          </summary>
          <p>UI Forge is an open-source library of reusable React components. Each component includes an example, installation command, usage code, and props documentation.</p>
        </details>

        <details class="faq-item group">
          <summary class="faq-summary">
            <span>How do I install a component?</span>
            <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
          </summary>
          <p>Open a component's documentation page and copy the installation command. Then copy the source into your project and adjust the imports or styling to fit your setup.</p>
        </details>

        <details class="faq-item group">
          <summary class="faq-summary">
            <span>Can I use the components commercially?</span>
            <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
          </summary>
          <p>Yes. You can use, modify, and ship the components in personal and commercial projects. Review the Terms page for the complete usage conditions.</p>
        </details>

        <details class="faq-item group">
          <summary class="faq-summary">
            <span>Can I customize the components?</span>
            <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
          </summary>
          <p>Absolutely. The components are intended as starting points. Change the classes, props, animation strength, colors, and structure to match your design system.</p>
        </details>

        <details class="faq-item group">
          <summary class="faq-summary">
            <span>Can I request a component?</span>
            <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
          </summary>
          <p>Yes. Open an issue or discussion in the project's GitHub repository with a description of the component and the interaction you need.</p>
        </details>

        <details class="faq-item group">
          <summary class="faq-summary">
            <span>What if I find a bug?</span>
            <span class="faq-icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
          </summary>
          <p>Please report it through GitHub with the component name, steps to reproduce, and your environment. Clear reproduction details make fixes much faster.</p>
        </details>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
